OL,3,GNEWSACharity shop helps to 'bankroll'
OL,4,Avillage carnival
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe organiser of one of the oldest
OL,7,Filluminated carnivals in the country
OL,8,Fsaid the event was only able to survive
OL,9,Ffinancially with the support of a local
OL,10,Fcharity shop.
OL,12,FPewsey Carnival - which started in 1898
OL,13,F- costs about #45,000 to run every
OL,14,Fyear, the majority of which is funded
OL,15,Fby Cossor's Shop in Pewsey, Wiltshire.
OL,17,FCarol Parsons, chair of the carnival,
OL,18,Fsaid the village was bucking the trend
OL,19,Fas funding issues have affected other
OL,20,Fcarnivals across the West and
OL,21,FTrowbridge Carnival had to be cancelled
OL,22,Fthis year.
OL,23,APub: 20-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
